Subject: [PATCH] virtio-pmem: Complete bio flushes when persistence is virtual

virtio-pmem can be backed by a VMM shared-memory window where the guest has a
usable pmem block device but the host cannot provide hardware-style write
pending queue persistence. The pmem driver already reports this as
"unable to guarantee persistence of writes"; in that mode, failing ordinary
REQ_PREFLUSH/REQ_FUA metadata writes turns the device from "best effort
persistence" into an unusable block device.

For bio-tied flushes, complete the request locally and let the block write
continue. Explicit region flushes still go through the virtio-pmem request
queue so freeze/shutdown paths can ask the host to make a best-effort sync.

--- a/drivers/nvdimm/nd_virtio.c
+++ b/drivers/nvdimm/nd_virtio.c
@@ -113,21 +113,11 @@ int async_pmem_flush(struct nd_region *nd_region, struct bio *bio)
 	/*
 	 * Create child bio for asynchronous flush and chain with
 	 * parent bio. Otherwise directly call nd_region flush.
 	 */
 	if (bio && bio->bi_iter.bi_sector != -1) {
-		struct bio *child = bio_alloc(bio->bi_bdev, 0,
-					      REQ_OP_WRITE | REQ_PREFLUSH,
-					      GFP_ATOMIC);
-
-		if (!child)
-			return -ENOMEM;
-		bio_clone_blkg_association(child, bio);
-		child->bi_iter.bi_sector = -1;
-		bio_chain(child, bio);
-		submit_bio(child);
-		return 0;
+		return 0;
 	}
 	if (virtio_pmem_flush(nd_region))
 		return -EIO;
 
 	return 0;
